A||||25||JC Webb||What mods can be done with $500||||5||
Z||000000||JC Webb||12-18-2000||08:48 PM||||I have a limited budget of $500 to spend on my 86 SE V-6 4-speed.  What do you all think are the best modifications in this price range?  Making my own turbo setup sounds like fun.  I have access to a lift if that helps!<BR>I already have Enkei wheels, short shifter, and an aftermarket chip.  Any help will be appreciated!||||reg||5
Z||000001||fropuff||12-18-2000||09:17 PM||||Nitrous; that's what I'm getting in the summer.  Pretty cheap performance.  May be a little more than that, but it'll be worth it.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||09:54 PM||||yep.. if your looking for instant success go the nitrous route..  but custom 2.5" exhaust ($200ish) MSD 6a ($130) Crane PS91 ($70) 8.8mm Accel wires ($50) all need to come with the nitrous.. not a must.. but they sure do help a lot. and Bigger injectors <A HREF="http://www.rceng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rceng.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||12-18-2000||09:55 PM||||I would spend my $500 on a good hi-pro Cam and port your Intake & exhaust manifolds and maybe some form of cold air intake (filter down in the wheel well) Or a NO2 kit but that could bite you in your ass on a stock engine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||12-18-2000||10:11 PM||||If you're into handling, how about lowering springs, KYB shocks, stiffer suspension bushings and sway bars?  Oops, I think I just ate more than $500.<P>Anyhow, better handling is like extra horsepower in the corners.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||12-18-2000||10:48 PM||||Brake upgrade. Not being able go fast is an inconvience, not being able to stop is a tragedy.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||12-18-2000||11:09 PM||||Geesh, with this question you will get 500 different opinions!<P>It depends on what your looking for.  Improved suspension, improved Hp, improved gas mileage, improved braking etc. etc.<P>I would save it for the next thing that goes wrong on your Fiero. I have found that when I blow 500 bucks on relatively useless and un-necessary mods, I end up needing it for repairs a couple miles down the road....<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||12-18-2000||11:32 PM||||I agree with that 100%... Your going to need repairs, so save your money.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Got2manyfieros||12-18-2000||11:52 PM||||I think I would opt for either headders, or koni shocks.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Slammed Fiero||12-19-2000||01:03 AM||||Go for suspension mods , Koni's , bars , springs , coil overs all a good start. Make the fiero handle like it should have.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000010||sqoach||12-19-2000||01:11 AM||||black88gt, johnnyk<BR>now that's not a very positive attitude to have about the fiero...keep your money to fix it cuz it's gonna break  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||12-19-2000||02:21 AM||||Beer.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||12-19-2000||02:31 AM||||Mr. Mikes Leather seats.<BR>Ported intake with a bored out throttle body and port out the exhaust manifolds.<BR>Stereo system.<BR>Springs and shocks/struts.<BR>Borla Exhaust.<BR>New wheels. (oops just reread you already have them...sorry)<BR>Better Tires.<BR>Meachum side scoops.<P>The possibilities are almost endless.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Carrolles||12-19-2000||06:47 AM||||The biggest bang for the buck suspension mod is the addition of a rear sway bar to a Fiero that does not have one.<P>An aftermarket one from JC Whitney runs around $125.00.  Installing a Fiero front bar on the rear runs around $25.00.  I picked up one for $10.00 and will get new bushings from AutoZone for around $15.00.<P>There is a good write-up on doing the install somewhere in the archives.  Take a look.<P>New oem shocks and struts will run around $100 if you install them yourself (it's not hard to do and the tools can be borrowed from AutoZone).<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||12-19-2000||08:26 AM||||NO!!! on the headers! don't waste your money! ported stock manifolds are $10 for the replacement gaskets and a saturday without your car. as for you having a problem with the NOs with a stock motor.. no you won't you'll be just fine... ||||reg||1
Z||000015||JohnnyK||12-19-2000||11:19 AM||||Sorry dude, just facing facts.. I say, buy the beer, wait for something to break.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||batboy||12-19-2000||04:10 PM||||I'm with Phil, Terry, Blackie, and Johnny. Do some brake upgrades, buy a bunch of beer, then use the leftover cash for repairs when it breaks down. For those of you who don't think Fieros breakdown occasionally, you haven't owned one very long.||||reg||1
Z||000017||batboy||12-19-2000||04:15 PM||||Ok, ok...Carrolles also has a good idea about the rear sway bar. Poly control arm bushings really make a diff too if you're into handling. I can't believe nobody but Oreif mentioned stereo mods. Ya need great sounding tunes for cruisin'!<P>I personally would never use nitrous unless I had forged pistons. Sure, plenty of people have used it without problems, but plenty of others have blown holes in the top of pistons too.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 12-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||elfiero||12-19-2000||04:25 PM||||spend 500 on the wife and she will let you<BR>spend 5 grand on the damn car! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000019||mshill||12-19-2000||05:48 PM||||$500 of beer only makes you think you're going faster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I was looking at the same budget after getting my 3.4L longblock.  Here's what I did:<P>1) Bored TB/Plenum to 57mm ($150+$20 shipping)<BR>2) Underdrive pulley ($80)<BR>3) Port stock exhaust manifolds ($5 grinding bits, $15 gaskets)<BR>4) Roller Rocker arms (1.5 or 1.6 ratio $120)<BR>5) Rear swaybar & bushings ($15 bushings)<BR>6) Accell SuperCoil ($40)<BR>7) 8mm wires ($40)<P>That comes pretty close to $500 right there.<BR>The other mod I am doing is the F-50 rebody ($6000) before paint, wheels and tires.||||reg||1
Z||000020||KRMFiero||12-19-2000||05:57 PM||||put it in stocks and in 20 years you will have about 1 million, by then you could by the nicest Fiero with a 2000 HP Jet engine on the back.. hell after about 20 years (putting a little bit away each year) you could buy the rights to the Fiero<P><BR>Kyle<P>Damn Consumer Math class, just makes me thing about stocks and crap<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||JC Webb||12-20-2000||06:13 PM||||Thanks everyone for your help!  I think I will tackle the suspension and grinding the exhaust manifolds first!  I was trying my best to ignore the repair stradegy, but that is a valid point.<P>JC Webb||||reg||10
